/*
    db.json5 - Seed data loaded on first run, when the User table is empty

    THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DEFINES NO USERS.

    It used to seed three accounts - admin, guest and super - all with the password "demo", and all
    three hashes were published in the source distribution. An integrator who followed every
    documented pre-deployment step still shipped a device with a known administrative password, and
    the "super" account, which holds the highest role in the hierarchy, was not mentioned in the
    README at all, so it was the one least likely to be noticed and removed.

    Create your own account instead. From the top of the Ioto source tree, after make, the password
    utility generates the BF1 hash. The hash covers the username and the realm ('web' unless
    web.json5 sets auth.realm or name):

        build/bin/password --cipher blowfish --realm web --password 'your-password' admin

    then add the record it prints here, or into your provisioning step:

        User: [
            {
                username: 'admin',
                password: 'BF1:...the hash bin/password printed...',
                role: 'admin',
            },
        ]

    The roles this app defines are in web.json5 under auth.roles.
 */
{
    User: [],
}
